---
/**
 * /review/ — the page that asks. One job, one button.
 *
 * WHY IT IS SEPARATE FROM /reviews/. That page is for a stranger deciding
 * whether to call us: fifteen quotes, the mechanics behind them, and a link
 * to the profile so they can check. This page is for somebody we have already
 * worked for, usually standing in their own driveway holding a phone. Those
 * are different readers wanting different things, and the second one was not
 * served at all — there was no "leave a review" link anywhere on this site
 * until 11 Nov 2026, while the owner's own short link sat unused in a comment
 * in business.ts.
 *
 * WHY THIS URL. The Map Pack guide of 11 Nov 2026 asked for "/review", and
 * short is the whole point: this address gets said out loud at a kitchen
 * table and typed into a phone with one hand. The old WordPress site had
 * /leave-a-review/, which has been redirecting to /contact/ and now comes
 * here instead — it carries a small amount of real search history.
 *
 * THE RULE THIS PAGE IS BUILT AROUND, and it is the same one as /reviews/.
 * 16 CFR Part 465 bans review gating: asking "how did we do?" first and then
 * routing the happy customers to Google and everybody else to a private
 * complaints form. This page offers both routes at once, to everyone, with
 * no question in front of either. That is deliberate and it is why the "call
 * us instead" section is not a smaller, quieter box at the bottom. If anybody
 * ever reorganizes this page so the review link appears only after a filter,
 * they have broken the law and not merely the design.
 *
 * NO REVIEW OR AGGREGATERATING MARKUP HERE EITHER, same reasoning as
 * /reviews/ — see the long note at the head of that file and the suppression
 * note in src/lib/schema.ts.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AnswerBox from '../components/AnswerBox.astro';
import LinkRail from '../components/LinkRail.astro';
import { business, isReady } from '../data/business';

const path = '/review/';

const answer =
  'If we have worked at your place and you are willing to say so publicly, the link on this page opens a Google review box for Sasquatch Pest Control. It takes about a minute. We offer nothing in exchange for one, we ask everybody the same way, and we do not screen who gets asked.';
---
<BaseLayout
  source="src/pages/review.astro"
  path={path}
  leadForm={false}
  title="Leave Us a Google Review"
  description="Leave a Google review for Sasquatch Pest Control of Bellingham. One link, about a minute. Nothing is offered in exchange and nobody is screened first."
  kind="page"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Leave a review', path }]}
>
  <h1>Leave us a Google review</h1>
  <AnswerBox text={answer} />

  {isReady(business.reviewUrl) && (
    <p class="review-ask">
      <a class="btn" href={business.reviewUrl as string} rel="nofollow noopener">
        Write a Google review
      </a>
    </p>
  )}

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What happens when you tap that</h2>

    <p>
      It opens Google&rsquo;s own review box for our Bellingham listing. You
      will need to be signed in to a Google account, because Google attaches
      every review to one — there is no version of this that skips that step,
      and if you are signed out you will see their sign-in page first rather
      than ours.
    </p>

    <p>
      What you write goes straight to Google. It does not come to us first, we
      cannot edit it, and we cannot take it down. It appears publicly under
      whatever name your Google account uses, and you can change or delete it
      yourself afterwards from the same place.
    </p>

    <p>
      A sentence or two is plenty. The ones that help somebody the most are the
      specific ones — which pest, which part of the county, whether the problem
      actually stayed gone.
    </p>

    <h2>If something went wrong, call us instead of writing it up</h2>

    <p>
      And we mean instead of, or before, or as well — whichever you like. A
      missed appointment or a treatment that did not hold is usually something
      we can put right the same week, and we would much rather hear it from you
      than read it later. Call or text
      <a href={`tel:${business.phoneE164}`}>{business.phone}</a>, or email
      <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Nothing here is conditional. The link above does not disappear if you
      call us first, and calling us does not buy you a quieter version of this
      page. Our
      <a href="/our-guarantee/">100% Service Guarantee</a> covers the return
      visit, and it has never been conditional on saying anything nice
      afterwards.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>We do not pay for reviews.</strong> No discount, no gift card,
        no entry in a drawing, no credit on the next visit.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>We do not screen anybody first.</strong> There is no
        &ldquo;how did we do?&rdquo; step in front of this link that sends the
        happy customers to Google and routes the unhappy ones somewhere
        private. That practice is called review gating and it is banned by the
        <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-16/chapter-I/subchapter-D/part-465" rel="nofollow noopener">FTC&rsquo;s
        rule on consumer reviews</a> (16 CFR Part 465).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>We do not write them.</strong> Not staff, not family, not an
        agency on our behalf.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>We do not try to have the bad ones removed.</strong> We reply
        to them.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The longer version of all of that, with the fifteen reviews we quote and
      the one we deliberately left out, is on
      <a href="/reviews/">our reviews page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <LinkRail
    heading="While you are here"
    links={[
      { href: '/reviews/', label: 'Read the reviews we quote, and how we got them' },
      { href: '/our-guarantee/', label: 'Our 100% Service Guarantee' },
      { href: '/contact/', label: 'Call, text or email us' },
    ]}
  />
</BaseLayout>
